(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Modules/_ctypes/_ctypes.c and stgdict.c: Copyright (c) the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License"] [4 1 "// Agreement for Python 3.14 (LICENSE.md). The port to Go: Copyright (c) the Arbace authors, under the same license."] [5 1 "//"] [6 1 "// The module _ctypes (queue 244; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 244\"; the user's 244-1 (a)): CPython"] [7 1 "// 3.14.10's types ported over pyi's objects, their memory the C world's (world.go), libffi's part ffi.go over ci."] [8 1 "// How the C maps onto Go here:"] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "//   - CDataObject is CData, a built-in value of one of the five base types (_SimpleCData, Structure, Union, Array,"] [11 1 "//     _Pointer, CFuncPtr); a Python class deriving from one (c_int, a Structure subclass) holds it in its instance"] [12 1 "//     (pyi's built-in subclass wrapper). b_ptr is an address of the world; b_objects, b_base, b_index, b_length,"] [13 1 "//     b_size are CPython's."] [14 1 "//   - StgInfo (stgdict.c) is kept per class in a table (stgs): CPython keeps it in the type object."] [15 1 "//   - The metatypes PyCSimpleType, PyCStructType, UnionType, PyCArrayType, PyCPointerType, PyCFuncPtrType are"] [16 1 "//     built-in subclasses of type: their __new__ makes the class by type.__new__ and then its StgInfo, as their"] [17 1 "//     tp_new and tp_init do; CDataType's methods (from_address, from_buffer, from_buffer_copy, from_param, in_dll,"] [18 1 "//     __mul__) are theirs."] [19 1 "//   - Structures are laid out by Lib/ctypes/_layout.py (3.14's), which makes the CField objects."] [31 1 "// StgInfo is stgdict.c's StgInfo."] [36 21 "// a simple type's _type_ (a str), an array's or a pointer's item type"] [40 23 "// a function pointer type's"] [49 21 "// __pointer_type__"] [50 21 "// simpleKind, structKind, ..."] [78 1 "// stgOf is PyStgInfo_FromType: t's StgInfo, or nil (an abstract class, or not a ctypes type)."] [87 1 "// CData is CDataObject."] [89 16 "// the base type (Type())"] [90 16 "// its class"] [95 17 "// its own memory, else nil (a base's, an address's)"] [96 17 "// b_base"] [98 17 "// b_objects"] [100 2 "// a function pointer's state (PyCFuncPtrObject)"] [102 2 "// exports counts the memoryviews of the object not released (queue 260, py's BufferExports): CPython's CDataObject"] [103 2 "// has no ob_exports and ctypes.resize refuses nothing, so nothing here calls Refuse; the count is memoryview's"] [104 2 "// managed buffer's"] [110 1 "// The buffer protocol (queue 260): PyCData_NewGetBuffer. The view's bytes are the object's memory in the C world, read"] [111 1 "// and written in place (b_ptr, b_size); its format is the StgInfo's (\"B\" when it has none: a union, an incomplete"] [112 1 "// structure), its shape the StgInfo's (ndim its length), its itemsize the size of the innermost item type of an array"] [113 1 "// (PyCData_item_type), else of the type itself; never read-only."] [117 1 "// BytesLike is the object's memory (the C world's, in place)."] [125 1 "// WritableBytes is the same memory for writing (view->readonly = 0)."] [133 1 "// BufferShape is the view's format, itemsize and shape."] [158 1 "// rawMemory is the exporter of memoryview_at's view (PyMemoryView_FromMemory): size bytes of the world at ptr, read-only"] [159 1 "// unless writable."] [186 1 "// withFn gives a function pointer instance its PyCFuncPtrObject state (one made from memory: a result, a field)."] [194 1 "// obj is c as a Python object (its class's instance)."] [202 1 "// cdataOf is the CData of o (a ctypes instance), or nil."] [232 23 "// ctypes.ArgumentError"] [241 1 "// _ctypes_simple_instance: true for a subclass of c_int and the like (its base is not _SimpleCData), false for"] [242 1 "// c_int itself (callproc.c: such a class is kept as an instance, not converted by its getfunc)."] [247 1 "// tpName is a type's tp_name as CPython prints it in these messages (its __name__ for a heap type)."] [250 1 "// newCData is generic_pycdata_new / PyCData_MallocBuffer: a zeroed instance of t of its own memory."] [263 1 "// baseKind is the built-in base of a ctypes class."] [274 1 "// fromBaseObj is PyCData_FromBaseObj: an instance of t on base's memory at adr (base nil: a copy of adr's bytes)."] [292 1 "// atAddress is PyCData_AtAddress: an instance of t over the memory at buf."] [303 1 "// container is PyCData_GetContainer."] [329 1 "// keepRef is KeepRef."] [343 1 "// cdataGet is PyCData_get."] [356 1 "// cdataSetInner is _PyCData_set."] [398 1 "// cdataSet is PyCData_set."] [407 1 "// extendError is _ctypes_extend_error: the exception err re-raised as cls with prefix and \"ExcType: msg\"."] [420 1 "// ---- the metatypes ----"] [422 1 "// initTarget is the class a metatype's __init__ initializes: the metatypes' tp_new is type.__new__ alone and their"] [423 1 "// tp_init makes the StgInfo, as CPython's (metacls.__new__ without __init__ gives an abstract class); the init runs the"] [424 1 "// creation functions below on the class already made, which newClass hands them."] [427 1 "// newClass is type.__new__ for a metatype's class (the class being initialized when a metatype's __init__ runs)."] [446 1 "// simpleTypeNew is PyCSimpleType_new and PyCSimpleType_init."] [469 3 "// 3.15 (queue 252; _ctypes.c's PyCSimpleType_init): _ctypes_get_fielddesc takes the complex types' \"Zf\", \"Zd\","] [470 3 "// \"Zg\", which pyi's ffi does not have (Py_FFI_COMPLEX_AVAILABLE false): one AttributeError, ctypes' import catches it"] [490 2 "// the swapped variant for the byte orders (__ctype_be__, __ctype_le__), as PyCSimpleType_init's create_other_endian_type"] [512 1 "// makeSwapped is create_other_endian_type: a class of the same name with the byte-swapped accessors."] [521 2 "// CPython passes the class's own namespace (its __qualname__ kept) and the name with st->swapped_suffix (queue 260)"] [543 1 "// fmtOf is the buffer format of a simple type's code (_ctypes_alloc_format_string_for_type)."] [545 2 "// queue 260: the standard-size code is ctypes' own but for i, I, l, L and ? (LP64, a 1-byte _Bool): c_char_p's"] [546 2 "// \"<z\", c_wchar's \"<u\", c_void_p's \"<P\" as CPython's"] [556 1 "// structTypeNew is PyCStructType_new/init (and UnionType's): the class, its StgInfo copied from its base's, its"] [557 1 "// _fields_ laid out when given."] [575 2 "// a class with _abstract_ in its namespace has no StgInfo (kept for compatibility: instantiating it is"] [576 2 "// \"abstract class\")"] [582 3 "// StructUnionType_init: PyObject_SetAttr, so a metaclass's __setattr__ sees them (queue 260: _endian.py's"] [583 3 "// _swapped_meta gives BigEndianStructure's fields their swapped types; pyi laid out the class's own)"] [592 1 "// updateStginfo is PyCStructUnionType_update_stginfo: the layout by ctypes._layout.get_layout, then the fields made"] [593 1 "// descriptors of the class (MakeAnonFields included)."] [697 2 "// the aggregate's ffi type (a union: its largest member's elements, stgdict.c's rule, as one struct)"] [704 2 "// a field of the class's own type marked it final during the layout (stgdict.c's check)"] [720 1 "// makeAnonFields is MakeAnonFields: the fields of each _anonymous_ field's type made the class's, at their offsets."] [748 1 "// makeFields is MakeFields: descr's type's fields as fields of t at offset."] [771 1 "// structTypeSetAttr is PyCStructType_setattro: _fields_ assigned lays the class out."] [790 1 "// arrayTypeNew is PyCArrayType_init."] [844 2 "// char and wchar_t arrays: value and raw"] [858 1 "// pointerTypeNew is PyCPointerType_new/init."] [876 1 "// pointerSetProto is PyCPointerType_SetProto: the item type, and the item type's __pointer_type__."] [883 2 "// PyCPointerType_SetProto: \"&\" and the item's format (\"B\" for an incomplete type), its shape before it (queue 260)"] [904 1 "// funcPtrTypeNew is PyCFuncPtrType_new/init: _argtypes_, _restype_, _flags_."] [961 1 "// converters is converters_from_argtypes: each argtype's from_param."] [977 1 "// ---- CDataType's methods (on the metatypes) ----"] [1030 3 "// CPython shares the buffer's memory; a Python buffer's bytes are Go memory, not the C world's: from_buffer"] [1031 3 "// copies them (a write through either is not seen by the other: the class :ctypes-buffer-share)"] [1139 1 "// arrayFromCtype is PyCArrayType_from_ctype: the class \"NAME_Array_N\", cached."] [1158 1 "// ---- CField ----"] [1229 20 "// a type used as a field's can no longer change its _fields_"] [1278 1 "// ---- instances ----"] [1280 1 "// simpleNew and genericNew are the types' tp_new."] [1323 1 "// structInit is Struct_init: positional arguments to the fields in order (the bases' first), keywords by name."] [1358 1 "// fieldNamesMRO: the names of the _fields_ of t and its bases, the bases' first (_init_pos_args)."] [1408 1 "// ---- arrays ----"] [1465 1 "// Slice_ is a slice's resolved indices."] [1542 1 "// ---- pointers ----"] [1605 1 "// ---- module functions ----"] [1627 1 "// CArgObject: byref's result, and from_param's."] [1630 15 "// the value's bytes (a pointer: 8)"] [1631 15 "// kept alive"] [1633 15 "// a struct by value: its address"] [1687 1 "// metaNew is a metatype's tp_new: type.__new__ alone."] [1690 1 "// metaInit is a metatype's tp_init: create (one of the creation functions) run on the class o."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[148 22] [204 41] [368 31] [381 38] [414 25] [429 20] [460 26] [462 35] [496 46] [499 47] [502 47] [505 48] [515 61] [518 58] [522 49] [523 46] [568 23] [577 49] [581 47] [584 46] [654 23] [684 49] [694 24] [741 55] [756 66] [764 49] [776 22] [780 47] [837 12] [837 38] [868 44] [898 19] [912 37] [921 40] [940 39] [945 52] [1010 35] [1043 28] [1047 36] [1072 35] [1101 34] [1141 31] [1263 27] [1264 20] [1265 28] [1282 20] [1334 41] [1344 48] [1351 38] [1377 35] [1419 34] [1448 26] [1483 14] [1483 24] [1489 14] [1489 24] [1496 12] [1496 22] [1519 78] [1519 99] [1526 51] [1567 45] [1571 32] [1608 21] [1611 20] [16